The story library brings together the "1+4" five categories of theme stories.
General Secretary Xi Jinping is the "first narrator of China's story", and the "learning" section is based on Xi Jinping's story, Xi Jinping's story, Xi Jinping's classic story and the story of Xi Jinping's favorite characters as the main line, providing a rich and convenient online platform for readers to learn the art of Xi Jinping's storytelling and realize the truth of governing the country; "governing the country", "struggling the dream", "Chinese culture" and " win-win cooperation".
The reporter learned from today's on-line press conference of "The United States and the United States - "China's good story" database held in Beijing that the "China good story" database has opened a Chinese and English website and a mobile phone client.
The content of the website is comprehensive, the function is rich, the design is fashionable, and the all-media shows a wonderful story.
The mobile phone client highlights the artificial intelligence voice function, adapts to the trend of mobile communication, and provides users with a "China good story" player.
In order to facilitate the use of queries, the database gives full play to the advantages of China's search intelligent search technology, providing rich search functions such as time search, map search, character search, and label search, which is convenient and easy to use.
â€œChina Good Storiesâ€ database has also specially set up an open content platform, which has opened a â€œstory numberâ€ for more than a dozen of the first resident units such as the SASAC.
Demonstrations to bomb the president's ouster of Egypt's mountains and rain, the authorities indicate a strong crackdown
Twitter hashtags and social media are motivating Egyptian people to take to the streets this day to peacefully demand President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi’s ouster.
However, the authorities have signaled their intention to use force against repression.
Since Sisi, the head of the military at the time, seized power in a military coup in 2013, the expression of dissent has almost disappeared in Egypt, and any form of protests will be put into extreme danger.
The Egyptian Center for Economic and Social Rights, a Cairo-based non-governmental organization, said more than 1,900 people had been arrested since a rare outburst of last weekend in protests calling for Sisi’s ouster.
Allegations of profligacy surrounding Sisi and his family’s profligacy for vanity led thousands of people to take to the streets.
Egypt's Ministry of the Interior firmly stated yesterday that any attempt to destabilise the country will be decisive and unscrupulous.
The center of Cairo has long been heavily guarded, with riot police, security agency vehicles and plainclothes police officers visible in the streets around Tahrir Square, the tipping point of the Egyptian revolution in 2011.
Al Jazeera reported that security forces detained a number of important scholars and social sages on the 25th, including political science professor at Cairo University and well-known columnist Nafa.
On the 24th, he tweeted: â€œI have no doubt that it will be a disaster to continue Sisiâ€TMs Absolute Dominion.â€
“It’s in Egypt’s interest for him to step down immediately.”
Prior to Nafa’s arrest, Hosni, a spokesman for Egypt’s former military chief of the military’s chief of staff, was taken into custody.
Nan was arrested last year after an attempt to run with Sisi for the presidency.
Davout, president of the Constitutional Party, has also been taken into custody.
Economists and politicians argue that at a time when economic woes among the poor and the middle class are intensifying, the crackdown on dissent reflects the government’s instability and fragility.
Ayman Nour, an opposition leader who once ran for the presidency, said: â€œThe crackdown underscores the regime's indifference to the Egyptian people and its own fear.â€
â€œBecause the economy has been ruined by him, coupled with widespread political repression, Sisi is trying to send a clear message to the important generals and politicians who may replace it.â€
Noor pointed out that under the premise that the socio-economic situation continues to deteriorate, the government's heavy-handed approach will only increase people's anger.
Now that the fear barrier has been dashed, he expects more people to take to the streets.
At the beginning of this month, Ali, a businessman and actor in exile in exile in Spain, began uploading a series of videos at the beginning of this month, claiming to benefit from government corruption and detonating small-scale demonstrations in different cities last weekend.
Mr. Ali said his company, Amrlak General, could get lucrative contracts without going through a statutory bidding process, underscoring the military’s corruptfulness to Sisi’s relatives, including first lady Intissar Amer al-Sisi.
He repented of his participation.
Ali claimed that he helped the palatial palatial palaces and luxury hotels of Sisiga, in stark contrast to the abstinence life of the current Egyptians, who had not yet paid.
On Twitter, themed hashtags such as â€œRour up, you are not aloneâ€ , â€œSisi youâ€ , â€œSisi are goneâ€, â€œSisiâ€ and â€œthe next Fridayâ€ have attracted tens of tens of thousands of tweets and reshoring, calling on the people to take to the streets in a peaceful manner to call for Sisi to step down.
Amarwick has nearly 7 million followers on Twitter.
He tweeted in Arabic yesterday: â€œSisi is destined to end... He’s done it, the people who support him are now making a big mistake.â€
The Hong Kong government has launched a free special training program to help employees who have recently been affected by the economy.
On the 27th, the Hong Kong SAR government announced the introduction of a free special training program for employees affected by the recent economic situation, and qualified trainees will receive a training allowance of HK$4,000 per month after completing the courses.
There are a lot of boutique customers in Hong Kong's Tsim Sha Tsui Harbour City.
Affected by the recent social disputes in Hong Kong, there has been a sharp decline in recent visits to Hong Kong, and in addition to the tourism industry, hotel, catering, retail and other industries have been affected.
The Secretary for Labour and Welfare of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) Luo Zhiguang and the Secretary for Commerce and Economic and Economic Development, Yau Tenghua, met with the media on entrusting the Employee Retraining Bureau to implement a special training program and measures to support the tourism industry.
The challenges facing Hong Kong’s economy are imminent and should not wait until the situation is calm.
Therefore, the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government has launched this free training program called “Special Love Value Added”.
According to reports, those who have been unemployed since June 1 or are required by their employers to take unpaid holidays will have the opportunity to participate in the plan as long as they meet the relevant requirements.
The most important part is "vocational skills" training, covering 19 industries, including tourism, retail and catering, there will also be new "innovative technology" courses, as well as cross-industry "universal skills" courses.
Yu Pengchun, chairman of the Employee Retraining Board, said that all courses are tuition-free, and it is expected that the plan can support about 10,000 people in need.
As long as the participants complete each full-time or part-time course, and the attendance rate reaches 80%, they will receive a special stipend with a maximum monthly allowance of HK$4,000 per participant.
According to reports, the training course is two to three months, provided by about 50 training institutions, the public will be able to report from October 3rd to March 31st next year, with a maximum of up to four courses per person.
In addition, the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government has also announced a series of measures to support the tourism industry and help the industry to overcome the difficulties.
These measures include the liberalization of funding for the tourism council, the subvention of 6000 tour guides to resume courses, and the exemption of travel agents from the annual fee.
Tired of exercise?
According to the Russian satellite network, a study of athletes shows that the brain will also show signs of fatigue after high-intensity exercise.
The study, led by Mathias Pésigril, an expert at the Pittier-Salpetri Hospital in France, shows that there’s an unobtvious link between mental and manual labor: both require cognitive control of activity.
“You need to be in control of an autonomous process in which muscles and joints aches can force yourself to stop.”
The study was initiated by the French National Institute of Sport and Physical Education (INSEP).
The school’s experts are responsible for preparing athletes for the Olympic Games.
Some athletes have begun to suffer from over-training syndrome, that is, they have an irrepressible feeling of tiredness after high-load exercise, the inability of the body to recover, and a decline in performance.
INSEP asks the question: Could part of the cause of this condition be neurofatigue, the kind of neurofatigue caused by excessive mental labor?
The study was published in the journal Current Biology.
A few days ago, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism and the China Art Museum to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China and specially curated the exhibition was finally unveiled.
Xu Beihong's "Peng Ma", Qi Baishi's "Peaceful Years", Li Keqing's "Wanshan red forest everywhere", Jing Shangyi's "Tajik Bride", Luo's neutral "father", Liu Wenxi's "four generations of ancestors and grandsons" more than 480 pieces of high-quality works, a collection of more than 20 important art museums in the country's classic collection, including almost all the classic works since the founding of China.
"Magnificent History Magnificent Painting - Celebrating the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China Fine Art Exhibition" rich and multi-dimensionally shows the great history and brilliant achievements of the 70th anniversary of the founding of the founding of the People's Republic of China, and showcases the unremitting fighting spirit and the great spirit of self-improvement.
The exhibition is divided into a prologue and four chapters.
The exhibition has a large-scale and well-receivable masterpiece, with more than 480 works on display, covering Chinese paintings, oil paintings, engravings, sculptures, watercolour water powders, annual paintings, promotional paintings and many other types of art, focusing on the classic works in the collection of Chinese art museums, bringing together the classic collections of more than 20 important academic institutions and art museums in China.
In addition, more than 130 new works of real-world themes organized by the Ministry of Culture and Tourism have just been completed for the first time.
In order to present the exhibition, for the first time, the China Art Museum called all the exhibition spaces in the whole museum, in addition to all the exhibition halls on the three floors of the museum, the outdoor courtyard space has also been transformed into a sculpture exhibition area, and through the exhibition design to form an internal and external exhibition pattern.
It is reported that the exhibition will be on display until November 2.
According to the unified arrangement of the activities to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China in Beijing, the China Art Museum was suspended from September 28 to October 1.
This year's theme is â€œTourism and Work: Building a better future for all â€œWorld Tourism Dayâ€ . The Tourism Bureau organizes a series of activities, including the reception of lucky travelers and traditional pallet competitions, to celebrate with residents and travellers.
On the same day, a special "World Tourism Day" celebratory dinner to promote exchanges with the tourism industry, the Director of the Department of Social Affairs and Culture Tan Jun Rong and others attended to participate in this global tourism event and actively promote the sustainable development of Macao's tourism industry.
On the same day, the head of the Tourism Bureau, Wen Qihua, and the deputy director, Xu Yaoming, and the relevant supervisors went to the Macao International Airport to send souvenirs to the lucky passengers of the World Tourism Day.
Mr. Wipoosiri, a traveler from Thailand who became the lucky traveler of the year, said he came to Macao about four to five times a year, and Macao is a suitable tourist destination for a large and small destination to enjoy Macao's food on weekend holidays as well as visiting the city of Macau.
Macao tourism mascot "Mei Mai" robot is also to welcome passengers, and the Passenger Enquiry Office under the Tourism Bureau also arranges to provide souvenirs to passengers throughout the day.
The traditional tray competition was held on the afternoon of the same day and gathered close to 180 participants, representing more than 29 hotels and restaurants in Macao respectively, which coincided with the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region this year.
There are also contestants wearing special costumes that match the return theme.
The contestants carried a bottle of "Macau beer" tray across the "Macau historical city" street, with the fastest speed to safely send the beer to the end of the kiosk, the process is intense, along the way to attract a large number of tourists to stop and take pictures and even cheer for the participants, showing the charm of Macao's tourism.
The men's team champion was won by Warren Obejas Cabada of the Macao Sands Center; the women's group champion was Ye Xiaoqing of Jiajing Group; the most special costume winners were Ou Huanming of Jiajing Group and Cui Zhihong of the Golden Dragon Hotel.
On the evening of the same day, the tourism bureau invited representatives of relevant departments, the industry and the media and hundreds of other guests to attend the World Tourism Day celebration dinner.
At the dinner, Tan Junrong said that he will return to the development of Macao's tourism industry in the past 20 years, but in the face of continuous changes in external environmental factors, the industry should be encouraged to make innovative thinking, on the basis of the success achieved, move forward, adjust the strategy and formulate new tourism products and promotion models, expand the market, and encourage the industry to continue to support the vigorous and sustainable development of Macao's tourism industry.
With the theme of â€œCelebrating the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Regionâ€, the dinner arranged for Macao singers to sing the local original congratulatory return song â€œLotus Oneâ€, as well as six large-scale tourism enterprises to present a number of performances on the theme of return, showing Macao's diversified tourism and leisure elements and the multi-talented side of tourism practitioners.
Since 1980, the World Tourism Organization has designated September 27 as World Tourism Day in order to promote the international community's understanding of the importance of tourism, especially its social, cultural, political and economic values.
The central bank carried out 30 billion yuan reverse repurchase operation
BEIJING, Sept. 27 (Xinhua) -- The People's Bank of China carried out a reverse repurchase operation of 30 billion yuan in the form of interest rate bidding on the 27th.
Because 40 billion yuan of reverse repurchases expired on the same day, the People's Bank of China's reverse repurchase operation achieved a net return of 10 billion yuan.
The central bank issued a notice saying that 30 billion yuan of reverse repo operations were carried out on the same day, with a period of 14 days and a winning interest rate of 2.7%.
This is the 7th consecutive working day of the central bank to carry out the 14-day-term reverse repurchase operation.
According to the Shanghai Interbank Offered Rate (Shibor), released on the 27th, the overnight interest rate was 1.313%, down 32.4 basis points from the previous trading day; the seven-day interest rate was 2.59%, up 1.3 basis points from the previous trading day; the 14-day interest rate was 2.95%, down by 1.7 basis points from the previous trading day; the one-year interest rate was 3.048%, which was the same as the previous trading day.
To make it more reassuring for Chinese citizens to "go out" - Cui Aimin, Consular Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
No matter where you go, the motherland is behind you.
On the 25th, the first foreign ministry consular protection public service film was launched, and this sentence at the end of the short film aroused the resonance of the majority of netizens.
In an interview with Xinhua News Agency, the Consular Affairs Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs Cui Aimin said that the short film aims to further let the public feel the feelings and temperature of "diplomacy for the sake of the people", so that Chinese citizens feel that no matter in any corner of the world, Chinese diplomats will lend a helping hand and give help, strength and hope.
It's no small thing to be safe overseas, just a leaf.
In the past 70 years, the number of "going out" by Chinese citizens has increased dramatically, from "less than one million per year" before the reform and opening-up period to more than 100 million per year today; at the same time, Chinese citizens' overseas travel safety is more secure, and the object of consular protection work and assistance has also expanded from overseas Chinese to various groups such as overseas Chinese, tourists, foreign students and migrant workers.
According to statistics, since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, we have organized and implemented more than 10 major actions to evacuate or transfer overseas Chinese citizens, and safely evacuated more than 40,000 Chinese citizens from dangerous and volatile areas.
It has accepted and coordinated the handling of about 500,000 cases of various types, involving nearly 1 million Chinese citizens.
In dangerous times, the motherland can take you home; want to come to a "walking trip" is no longer a dream.
As of the end of August this year, China has concluded mutual visa exemption agreements with 14 countries covering ordinary passport holders.
In addition, more and more and more countries have unilaterally granted Chinese citizens visa-free or visa-on-arrival facilities.
42 countries and regions, such as Thailand and Egypt, have unilaterally granted visa-on-arrival visas to Chinese citizens holding ordinary passports, and 15 countries and regions such as Indonesia have unilaterally granted visa-free entry to Chinese citizens with ordinary passports.
In addition to visa-free and visa-on-arrival arrangements, it is becoming more and more convenient for Chinese citizens to apply for visas, and the formalities are becoming more and more simplified.
As of the end of August, China has reached agreements or arrangements with 41 countries to simplify visa formalities.
These include agreements with the United States, Canada, Israel, and Argentina to issue 10-year valid multi-time visas for mutual tourism and business personnel, and two-year multi-visa arrangements with the United Kingdom for each other's tourism, business and family visits.
The United Kingdom and Belgium have jointly launched a "one-stop visa" service, and France, Italy and Singapore have shortened the visa processing time to 48, 36 and 24 hours respectively.
For business people who often go abroad, the APEC business travel card with multiple entry and convenient customs clearance is a good choice.
Holding the travel card is equivalent to five-year-old multiple visas from 16 economies around the Asia-Pacific region, which is of great significance for business personnel, especially private enterprise personnel to "go out".
At present, China's effective cardholders rank first among APEC economies.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs will earnestly discuss the bilateral visa reciprocity agreement, encourage more countries to adopt visa facilitation measures for Chinese citizens, transform the achievements of diplomatic work into measures to benefit and benefit the people, and continuously improve the "golden content" of Chinese passports.
The National Day is approaching.
On the morning of yesterday, the Municipal Party Secretary Cai Qi led the team to check the safe production and holiday market supply during the National Day.
He stressed that it is necessary to improve the political position, strengthen the bottom-line thinking, do a solid and detailed job, ensure the safe operation of the city and the supply of the market, welcome the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China, and let the public have a happy and peaceful festival.
The deputy secretary of the municipal party committee and the mayor Chen Jining checked together.
With an area of nearly 7 square kilometers, the power supply service center in the Tian'anmen region has built an intelligent inspection system to carry out real-time monitoring and analysis of the data to achieve intelligent operation and maintenance of equipment, evaluation and security.
